# Toyota Yaris XP10 three-door hatchback, 1999-2005.
#
# The first-generation Yaris, the car that replaced the Starlet in Britain and
# won European Car of the Year. UK on sale 8 April 1999 at £7,495 for the entry
# car, up to £10,995 on the road, and replaced by the XP90 in January 2006.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/the-new-toyota-yaris-2/
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Gen1-Yaris-archive-press-pack.pdf
#
# Dimensions 3.615 x 1.660 x 1.500 m, wheelbase 2.370 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Vitz", first-generation XP10 infobox: wheelbase 2,370 mm,
# length 3,615 mm for 1998-2001 and 3,640 mm for 2001-2005, width 1,660 mm,
# height 1,500 mm for front-wheel drive. The 3.615 m figure is modelled because
# the photographs are of the early shape. The hull measures 3.615 x 1.660 m on
# a 2.370 m wheelbase, 65.6 per cent. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.828 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack holds a rear-left three-quarter of a red three-door,
# a front-right three-quarter of a gold three-door and a rear view of the same
# gold car, plus one interior photograph that carries no body information and
# was excluded. No true side elevation exists, so the flank was built from the
# photographs with the wheel centres fixed by the published ratio. Both cars
# are the pre-facelift three-door, and that is what is modelled.
#
# Colours: no Toyota GB colour list for the 1999-2004 car was found. The names
# used here are the Toyota GB brochure names for the 2005 model year, evidence
# grade (a), applied to the earlier car as the nearest documented British
# palette: Crystal Silver, Cirrus White, Eclipse Black, Chilli Red. Weights
# silver 3, white 3, red 2, black 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h, between the 1.0-litre car's 155 and the 1.3-litre car's
# quoted maximum. Comfort 65/280, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 65: small and light,
# but well built and quiet for its class. Classes 0,1,2, because it was cheap
# enough to be the first car of a low-income household and drifted down the
# bands as it aged.
#
# Dates are road presence: April 1999 intro, retires staggered 2011-2014 on a
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp10.dae (75 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-yaris-xp10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear pillar is broader than the photographs, the
# headlamp outlines are angular rather than rounded, and the hatch perimeter
# and bumper contours are less defined. The top view and the eight-view turn
# confirm a continuous body-coloured roof. At 128 px the tall body, the short
# overhangs and the rounded nose read as the first Yaris.

obj=citycar
